+# Changes Made to Remove Statsmodels Dependency
+
+## Summary of Changes
+
+1. **Modified `category_encoders/glmm.py`**:
+   - Added conditional import for statsmodels with try/except block
+   - Added checks in `__init__` and `_fit` methods to raise informative ImportError when statsmodels is not available
+   - Users can still import GLMMEncoder but will get clear error messages when trying to use it
+
+2. **Updated `requirements.txt`**:
+   - Removed statsmodels from the dependency list
+   - Project can now be installed without statsmodels
+
+3. **Updated `tests/test_glmm.py`**:
+   - Added conditional import check for statsmodels
+   - Added `@unittest.skipUnless` decorators to skip GLMM tests when statsmodels is not available
+   - Tests pass gracefully when statsmodels is not installed
+
+4. **Added documentation**:
+   - Created README.statsmodels.md explaining the optional dependency
+   - Error messages guide users on how to install statsmodels if needed
+
+## Behavior After Changes
+
+- **Without statsmodels**: GLMMEncoder can be imported but raises helpful ImportError when used
+- **With statsmodels**: GLMMEncoder works exactly as before
+- **Other encoders**: Continue to work normally without any changes
+- **Test suite**: Passes completely when statsmodels is not available (GLMM tests are skipped)
+
+## Installation Options
+
+Users who need GLMM functionality can install statsmodels separately:
+```bash
+pip install statsmodels
+```
+
+This approach makes statsmodels an optional dependency while maintaining backward compatibility for users who have it installed.
